WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.160
Dean, bro, you went back in the past.

00:02.160 --> 00:03.280
Come on, bro.

00:03.280 --> 00:07.440
Listen, I was so excited too, because I'm pretty sure

00:07.440 --> 00:10.720
you play the trombone, and I'm out here playing

00:10.720 --> 00:12.480
the sous-a-phone in my local.

00:12.480 --> 00:13.320
You are?

00:13.320 --> 00:13.840
Yeah.

00:13.840 --> 00:14.840
Yeah, so.

00:14.840 --> 00:15.320
Really?

00:15.320 --> 00:17.080
Where are you in Tensee?

00:17.080 --> 00:19.320
What is the band?

00:19.320 --> 00:21.720
We're called the Knoxville Honkers and Bangers.

00:21.720 --> 00:23.480
Our band is less than a year old.

00:23.480 --> 00:25.120
We are a brand new.

00:25.120 --> 00:27.480
The Providence version of the Honk Festival,

00:27.480 --> 00:29.600
I was on the planning committee for like five years

00:29.600 --> 00:30.600
in a row.

00:30.600 --> 00:33.480
I was in a couple different bands.

00:33.480 --> 00:35.360
The band called Extroder and Edition Band

00:35.360 --> 00:37.440
in a band that's called Under-Tone.

00:37.440 --> 00:39.880
Now used to be called What's Here.

00:39.880 --> 00:41.040
I was in a couple of them.

00:41.040 --> 00:41.720
I loved it.

00:41.720 --> 00:44.720
This is my life for one chunk of my life.

00:44.720 --> 00:46.440
And loved it.

00:46.440 --> 00:48.200
It just got to make the t-shirt that year.

00:48.200 --> 00:53.920
So I just wanted to show some people who might be there.

00:53.920 --> 00:57.400
The person playing some bulls is in my band.

00:57.400 --> 00:59.160
Some of these people, I think this is a player

00:59.160 --> 01:03.360
that's like negatively taken from pictures of Honk.

01:03.360 --> 01:05.080
Just like sketch.

01:05.080 --> 01:08.880
But yeah, it was really, that was a big chapter in my life.

01:08.880 --> 01:09.680
I don't know.

01:09.680 --> 01:13.280
I already liked Pink and Red and Purple at that point.

01:13.280 --> 01:16.480
So I was wondering where all you all played music.

01:16.480 --> 01:21.960
What qualified someone as a community activist street band?

01:21.960 --> 01:25.200
I think people have questions about that.

01:25.200 --> 01:29.120
Like I've played like, I'm pretty sure

01:29.120 --> 01:31.600
every played and abortion rights,

01:31.600 --> 01:33.640
one of the bands played in abortion rights rally.

01:33.640 --> 01:36.080
And I've definitely been with my bandmates

01:36.080 --> 01:40.840
like going down to like where the prison is like in Rhode Island

01:40.840 --> 01:43.520
and playing like outside so people could hear us.

01:43.520 --> 01:46.280
And like I've done a lot of things like that.

01:46.280 --> 01:51.080
But I think there definitely is within the community

01:51.080 --> 01:54.880
like some split around like what does it really mean

01:54.880 --> 01:55.840
to be activist.

01:55.840 --> 01:58.160
I think some of them, they're,

01:58.160 --> 02:00.480
that I think there are some bands

02:00.480 --> 02:02.960
where like literally the only thing that they do

02:02.960 --> 02:05.120
is play activist events.

02:05.120 --> 02:08.160
And then I think under to a brass band,

02:08.160 --> 02:11.600
we played like a regular show

02:11.600 --> 02:13.680
but also would play activist events.

02:13.680 --> 02:16.440
And then I think a story or an edition band

02:16.440 --> 02:19.480
would play like more so.

02:19.480 --> 02:21.360
I think mostly like community events.

02:21.360 --> 02:22.720
I feel like mostly.

02:22.720 --> 02:25.040
Yeah, I think people talked about it in the group.

02:25.040 --> 02:26.760
Like are we doing enough to qualify

02:26.760 --> 02:28.280
as like an activist rebound?

